"The surah begins with disjointed letters (huruf al-muqatta'at) such as Alif-Lam-Ra. These letters are a secret known to Allah and demonstrate the miraculous nature of the Quran. There are different views regarding their meaning: some have stated that they signify meanings such as 'I am the Lord' or 'I am Allah, I see.' However, the most appropriate view is that these letters are ambiguous (mutashabih) and that their true meaning must be left to Allah. Furthermore, these letters serve as the name of the surah, draw attention to the power of deriving boundless meanings from limited letters, and indicate that the Quran is a divine book.\n\nThe annexation of the verses to the whole Book indicates that this surah is a part of that wise Book. The attribute 'Hakim' conveys the meanings that the Quran is full of wisdom, decisive (muhkam), giving judgment, and being governed by wisdom. The Quran is a book filled with divine wisdom, serving as a basis for judging with justice and goodness, and protected from corruption. This surah is also among the verses of that Book and contains divine secrets and wisdom that confound the disbelievers.\n\nPeople found it strange that revelation should come to a man from among human beings and said, 'This is an evident magician.' Yet this is a grace from Allah. The 'qadam-i sidq' (footing of truth)—that is, the station of truthfulness—granted to the Prophet expresses his high rank in the sight of Allah and his authority of intercession. For the believers, this is great glad tidings. It is the disbelievers' viewing of this matter as strange and calling it sorcery that is truly astonishing, for choosing the prophet from among human beings is full of wisdom in terms of establishing familiarity with them.\n\nYour Lord is Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth in six days, then established Himself above the Throne (istiwa) and directs all affairs. No one can intercede without His permission. Such is Allah, your Lord; so worship Him. And to Him is your return. Allah originates creation, then repeats it in order to reward with justice those who believe and do righteous deeds. As for the disbelievers, for them is a drink of scalding water and a painful punishment.\n\nAllah made the sun a radiant light (diya, a source of light) and the moon a reflected light (nur). He determined phases for the moon so that you might know the number of years and the calculation of time. He created these in truth; it is not in vain. In the alternation of night and day, and in all that is created in the heavens and the earth, there are indeed many signs for a people who are mindful of Allah. These signs point to Allah's existence, oneness, and power.\n\nThe word haqq is used in various meanings, such as the correspondence of thought to reality, and the conformity of word and deed to purpose. Allah Almighty, through His name 'al-Haqq,' is the supreme Being worthy of His own Essence, Whose existence is necessary, and Who is free from every deficiency. Everything other than Him cannot exist on its own; rather, they exist only through Allah's creation and for Him, and in this respect they are termed 'haqq li-ghayrihi' (true/real through another). It is stated that the heavens, the earth, and what is between them were created in truth and according to a specified term.\n\nIn the alternation of night and day and in everything created in the heavens and the earth, there are many signs for a people who fear disobeying Allah. Divine signs are understood by those endowed with knowledge, and these guide a person to reflect upon the reckoning of the Hereafter and to observe truth and justice. Allah explains His verses in detail for a people who know.\n\nThe destination of those who do not expect to meet Allah, who are pleased with the life of this world and content with it, and who are heedless of Our verses, is Hellfire on account of what they used to earn. As for those who believe and perform righteous deeds, their Lord guides them by virtue of their faith, and rivers flow beneath them in the Gardens of Delight (Jannat an-Na'im). Their supplication therein will be glorification (tasbih), their greeting will be peace (salam), and the end of their prayer will be: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\n\nIf Allah were to hasten the evil for people as they wish the good to be hastened, He would have brought their appointed term upon them immediately. But He leaves those who do not expect to meet Him wandering blindly in their transgression. When adversity touches a person, he supplicates Allah in every posture; yet when the adversity is removed, he behaves as if he had never supplicated Him. Earlier generations were also destroyed because they opposed their prophets; and you have been made successors after them so that it may be seen how you will act.\n\nWhen the verses were recited, those who did not expect to meet Allah said, 'Bring a Quran other than this, or change it.' The Prophet declared that he could not change it of his own accord, but only followed what was revealed to him. Who is more unjust than one who invents a lie against Allah or denies His verses? Mankind was originally a single community, but then they fell into dispute; had a decree from your Lord not preceded, judgment would already have been passed between them. They demand a miracle; say, 'The unseen belongs only to Allah.'\n\nAllah is the One Who enables you to travel on land and sea. When you are in ships, sailing along with a favorable breeze and rejoicing in it, a violent storm suddenly strikes, waves surround them from every side, and they think they are doomed. Then they cry out to Allah in complete sincerity, saying, \"If You save us from this, we will surely be among the grateful.\" Yet when Allah saves them, they commit injustice upon the earth. O people! Your insolence is only against yourselves. Enjoy the fleeting pleasure of worldly life; then to Us is your return, and We will inform you of what you used to do.\n\nWhen Our verses are recited to them, those who dislike the truth say, \"Bring a Quran other than this, or change it.\" This is because they wish to alter the verses they dislike. Say to the Prophet: \"It is not for me to change it of my own accord; I follow only what is revealed to me. If I disobey my Lord, I fear the punishment of a tremendous Day.\"\n\nIf they say, \"This is your own word,\" say: \"Had Allah willed, I would not have recited it to you, nor would He have made it known to you. I lived among you for a lifetime before this; I was entirely illiterate and composed no poetry. Will you not use your reason?\" This is clear proof that the Quran is a revelation.\n\nWho could be more unjust than one who invents a lie against Allah or denies His verses? The criminals will never prosper. They worship idols that can neither harm nor benefit them, and say, \"These are our intercessors with Allah.\" Say: \"Do you inform Allah of something He does not know in the heavens or on the earth?\" Exalted is Allah above what they associate with Him.\n\nMankind was originally a single community, then they fell into dispute. Had a decree from your Lord not preceded, judgment would have been rendered among them immediately regarding that over which they differed. Those who do not expect to meet Allah say, \"Why has a sign not been sent down to him from his Lord?\" Say: \"The unseen belongs only to Allah. So wait; indeed, I am with you among those who wait.\"\n\nWhen We let people taste mercy after adversity has afflicted them, they immediately plot against Our verses. Say: \"Allah is swifter in scheming.\" Indeed, Our messengers are recording what you devise.\n\nAllah is the One Who enables you to travel on land and sea, gives you mobility, and removes obstacles. While sailing in ships with a pleasant wind, suddenly a storm arrives and waves encompass you. It is then that you forget what you previously worshipped and plead only with Allah, promising that if He delivers you, you will certainly be among the grateful. This is an example of man turning to Allah in times of distress.\n\nYet when Allah delivers you from that distress, you immediately begin to commit injustice upon the earth. You forget your promise, transgress, and rebel. However, this insolence of yours harms only yourselves; you enjoy a temporary benefit in the world, then your return is to Us, and We will inform you of what you used to do.\n\nThe likeness of the life of this world is like this: We send down rain from the sky, with which the plants grow and the earth is adorned. While people think they have full power over it, Our command comes suddenly by night or by day, and We devastate it as if nothing had existed there yesterday. Thus do We explain the verses for a people who reflect.\n\nAllah calls to the home of peace (Paradise) and guides whom He wills to a straight path. For those who do good is the best reward and even more; neither gloom nor humiliation will cover their faces. They are the people of Paradise, abiding therein eternally. As for those who earn evil deeds, they are recompensed with the like thereof, and humiliation covers them; their faces become like a dark night. They are the people of Hell, abiding therein eternally.\n\nOn that Day, We will gather the polytheists and those they associated with Allah. We will separate them, and their partner-gods will say, \"You did not worship us; we were unaware of your worship.\" Right there, everyone will face what they did, and they will be returned to Allah, their true Master (Mawla), and whatever they used to invent will vanish from them.\n\nSay to them: Who provides for you from the heaven and the earth? Who created and controls your senses of hearing and sight? Who brings out the living from the dead, and the dead from the living? Who regulates all affairs? They will say, \"Allah.\" Will you not then fear Allah? That is Allah, your true Lord. So what is there after truth except error? How then are you turned away from the truth?\n\nThe word of your Lord has come true against the transgressors who strayed from the true religion: they will never believe. Say: Is there among your associate-gods any who originates creation and then reproduces it? Allah originates creation and then reproduces it. How then are you turned away? Who guides to the right path? Allah guides to the truth. Is, then, He who guides to the truth more worthy of being followed, or he who cannot find the way unless guided? Most of them follow nothing but conjecture, and conjecture can never take the place of truth in any way. Indeed, Allah is fully aware of what they do.\n\nRegarding the question of creation, people of understanding must grasp this reality: it is impossible for contingent beings to create one another in an infinite chain. For every created thing requires a preceding cause to exist. One must find a power that breaks this chain and serves as the First Cause, which can only be Allah, who exists by His own Essence and has no need of anything. For this reason, searching for the first creator among created beings is futile. Allah originates creation from the very beginning and then reproduces it. He brings out the living from the dead and the dead from the living; He brings into being brand-new creations that transcend the laws of nature. In the face of this reality, falling into polytheism (shirk) is plain astraying.\n\nThe situation is the same regarding knowledge and discernment (marifah): no being other than Allah can independently guide to the truth. Reason and the senses are not creators of knowledge, but merely its perceivers. The harmony between subject and object is only possible through the guidance of Allah, who is above all things. In the history of philosophy, this issue has taken shape around three main views: those who argue for the impossibility of knowledge like the Sophists; those who absolutize reason like the idealists; and those who reduce everything to matter like the materialists. All of them failed to escape contradiction. The true judgment, however, is realized only through the guidance of Allah.\n\nWhile these proofs are evident, most of the polytheists turn away from the truth and follow nothing but conjecture. Yet conjecture can never take the place of truth. Allah knows all that they do and will punish them. The proofs of existence and knowledge are clear demonstrations of Allah's knowledge and power.\n\nAnd this Quran could not possibly be fabricated by anyone besides Allah. It confirms the scriptures before it and explains everything in detail. There is no doubt about it. If the polytheists say, \"The Prophet fabricated it,\" challenge them: \"Then bring forth a surah like it, and call upon whomever you can besides Allah for help.\" They cannot do this, because this Book is divine speech.\n\nThey denied the Quran, whose knowledge they could not encompass and whose interpretation (ta'wil) had not yet reached them. Those before them did the same, and terrible was their end. Some of them will believe, and some will not believe. Your Lord knows best the corruptors. If they deny you, say: \"For me is my deed, and for you is your deed. What you do cannot harm me, and what I do cannot benefit you.\"\n\nAmong them are those who listen to you, but can you make the deaf hear? And among them are those who look at you, but can you guide the blind? Allah does not wrong people in the least; rather, people wrong themselves. On the Day when Allah gathers them, it will be as if they had remained in the world for only a very short time. Those who denied meeting Allah will suffer the greatest loss.\n\nEvery community has a messenger. When their messenger comes, judgment is delivered between them with justice. They seek to hasten the punishment. Say: \"If His punishment should come to you by night or by day, what would you say?\" Will you believe only after the punishment has fallen? By then, it will be too late. Then it will be said to the wrongdoers: \"Taste the eternal punishment!\" This is the recompense for what you used to earn.\n\nThe polytheists were asking our Prophet (peace be upon him) whether the punishment was real. Allah Almighty commands him to say that, by my Lord, the punishment is an absolute truth and none of them will be able to escape it. On that Day, everyone who did wrong, upon seeing the punishment, would want to ransom all that is on earth if they owned it, and they will feel remorse deep inside. Yet judgment will be delivered between them with justice, and none will be wronged. Whatever is in the heavens and the earth belongs to Allah. His promise will surely come to pass, but most people do not know. He is the One who gives life and causes death, and to Him everyone will be returned.\n\nAllah Almighty has sent down the Quran to humanity as an admonition, a healing for the hearts, and a guidance and mercy for the believers. Our Prophet is commanded to tell them to rejoice in Allah's grace and mercy, for this is better than all that they amass. The polytheists were determining lawful and unlawful from the provisions Allah sent down according to their own whims. Yet they had no permission from Allah in this regard, and indeed they were fabricating lies against Allah. Allah has bestowed immense bounty upon mankind, but most of them do not give thanks. Furthermore, whatever work a person engages in, or whatever they recite from the Quran, Allah is a witness over it. Not even an atom's weight on earth or in heaven escapes your Lord; all is recorded in a clear book.\n\nFor the friends of Allah (awliya Allah), there is no fear, nor shall they grieve. They are those who believe and remain conscious of Allah and guard against evil (ittaqaw). For them are glad tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. There is no change in the words of Allah, and that is the supreme triumph. The miraculous gifts (karamat) of the friends of Allah are true; they are people who love one another for the sake of Allah and remind others of Allah when seen. They demonstrate their love through worship and obedience to Allah, and Allah demonstrates His friendship to them through miraculous gifts. In these verses, the definition of the friends of Allah is given, and it is emphasized that they are free from fear and sorrow.\n\nThe words of the polytheists should not grieve the Prophet (peace be upon him); for all honor belongs to Allah. He hears and sees all things. Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth belongs to Allah. Those who worship others besides Allah do not truly follow their associate-gods; they follow only conjecture and they do nothing but lie. Allah created the night for rest and the day for seeing and working. In this, there are lessons for a people who listen. The polytheists ascribed offspring to Allah; He is exalted above this and is free of all need. They have no proof for this. Those who invent falsehood against Allah cannot attain salvation; their worldly pleasures will quickly end, then their return is to Allah, and they will taste the severe punishment for their disbelief.\n\nThe story of Noah (Nuh) is recounted: He told his people that he relied on Allah, that they and their associates could do whatever was in their power without giving him any respite, and stated that he asked no fee from them. When his people denied him, Noah and those with him in the ark were saved, while those who disbelieved were drowned. Afterwards, many prophets were sent with clear miracles, yet their peoples continued to deny them. Allah seals the hearts of the transgressors. Moses (Musa) and Aaron were sent to Pharaoh and his assembly, but they displayed arrogance against the truth and called it obvious magic. Moses confronted the magicians, and Allah nullified their magic. Out of fear of Pharaoh, only a small number of people believed in Moses; nevertheless, the Children of Israel were ultimately guided across the sea, and although Pharaoh professed faith as he was drowning, this faith was not accepted. His corpse was preserved as a warning for future generations.\n\nThe Prophet (peace be upon him) was told to ask those who read the scripture before him if he were in doubt concerning the revelation sent down to him; yet it was emphasized that the truth had come to him from his Lord and that he must not be among the doubters. Those who deny Allah's verses suffer loss. Those against whom the decree of their Lord has been fulfilled will not believe, even if all miracles were to come to them, until they see the painful punishment. However, when the people of Jonah (Yunus) believed, the humiliating punishment in worldly life was lifted from them, and they were granted comfort for a time. This is an exception showing that their faith benefited them.\n\nDisbelievers do not believe until the punishment befalls them. However, believing once they see the punishment does not benefit them. For faith at the moment of despair is not acceptable.\n\nThe people of the prophet Jonah are the exception to this. They believed before seeing the punishment, and Allah lifted the worldly punishment from them. This shows that their faith was accepted.\n\nIf Allah had willed, He could have made everyone believe. However, compelling people to believe is not the prophet's duty. Faith occurs only by Allah's permission. And those who do not use their reason are condemned to punishment.\n\nLooking at the signs in the heavens and the earth is useless for those who do not believe. They await disasters similar to those that befell earlier peoples. Allah will save His prophets and the believers.\n\nThe Prophet declares that he will not worship anything other than Allah and that he will remain devoted to the religion of monotheism (tawhid). Help is sought from Allah alone; none other than Him can cause either benefit or harm. Allah bestows mercy upon whomever He wills.\n\nThe truth has come to humanity. Whoever chooses the right path does so for his own good, and whoever goes astray does so to his own loss. The Prophet is not a guardian over them. Obeying the revelation and being patient have been commanded."